{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1192102-on-resolving-paradox-conditions","id":1192102,"title":"On Resolving Paradox Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-05T18:39:27-08:00","id":1192102,"title":"On Resolving Paradox Conditions","content":"I find the language in the &quot;Paradox Conditions&quot; section of the core book a little confusing, at least in the layout; Can Paradox Conditions be scoured out of one's pattern at any time, or only after they lapse? Also, it says that scouring them out yields up an Arcane Beat, but is mum on the rewards for the 'accepting the consequences' route. Would that be an Arcane Beat also, or an actual Beat? Or would it be the player's choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T18:57:03-08:00","id":1192109,"title":"","content":"I believe that resolving a Paradox Condition before it lapses would be a regular Beat, the same as resolving any other Condition, they're generally more broadly applicable than Arcane Beats. Scouring the Condition before it lapses is probably an option since that achieves the goal of lapsed Paradox Condition but faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:16:40-08:00","id":1192131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1192102-on-resolving-paradox-conditions#post1192102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the language in the &quot;Paradox Conditions&quot; section of the core book a little confusing, at least in the layout; Can Paradox Conditions be scoured out of one's pattern at any time, or only after they lapse? Also, it says that scouring them out yields up an Arcane Beat, but is mum on the rewards for the 'accepting the consequences' route. Would that be an Arcane Beat also, or an actual Beat? Or would it be the player's choice?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936\">This is a recurring question, and my answer to it remains largely unchanged</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9